## Bandit Level 9  → Level 10 

**Challenge:** 
The password for the next level is stored in the file data.txt in one of the few human-readable strings, preceded by several ‘=’ characters.

**Solution:**
bandit9@bandit:~$ strings data.txt | grep "="
FB`=
c\5D=
========== the
?/=l
=Uc1
=vG*2P
========== password
k=ezG
E========== is
=%r_
.?=Dm
O&A=n
5========== FGUW5ilLVJrxX9kMYMmlN4MgbpfMiqey
=*^Y
=L3jT
q<=,
'QHE=
+=NBf

**Explanation:**
First I used the file command on data.txt to find out what type of file it was and since it was data I then used the strings command to get the human readable text and then pipe it into the grep command to search for lines with = thus giving me the password.


**Password:**
FGUW5ilLVJrxX9kMYMmlN4MgbpfMiqey

**What I learned:**
strings is good to give you the human readable text in a file and can also be used in conjunction with a lot of other commands like grep in this instance to give me the desired output.










